# Vendored third-party assets: never touch their bytes.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this repo, which would rewrite line endings in
# Font Awesome's CSS and LICENSE.txt on checkout. For files copied verbatim from
# an upstream release that is wrong twice over - it makes the working copy differ
# from what was committed, and it edits a licence file.
static/fontawesome-free/** -text

# The licence text, verbatim from gnu.org. Same reasoning: git should not be
# rewriting the bytes of a licence.
LICENSE -text
